Original scirpt (hostfile-topologify.org.py) is downloaded from:
  https://code.amazon.com/packages/ElasticCollectivesMiscScripts/blobs/mainline/--/hostfile-topologify.py

We need to accommodate ec2-topology-aware-for-slurm in FS cluster:
  https://github.com/aws-samples/ec2-topology-aware-for-slurm

Meanwhile, this is "how to topologify"

1. Install necessary packages
$ pip3 install boto3 pyopenssl # if not installed

2. Prepare a fixed group of nodes, e.g.
$ salloc --nodes=64 --job-name=<YOUR_ALIAS> --exclusive --partition dev 

3. Create a host file
$ scontrol show hostnames $(squeue --jobs ${JOBID} --noheader --format %N) > hosts

4. Topologify
$ python3 hostfile-topologify.py --output hosts.topologify --input hosts
